 # Week 5 — Phase 7 defects and verification
 
+## 4 November 2026 — Android/iPhone GATT 133 retry investigation
+
+### Offer session-binding completion race — follow-up implementation
+
+Deterministic production-coordinator/fake-frame test reproduces the exact
+`Rescue response session binding is invalid` error when the remote receives
+a signed proof response before the local native write-completion callback.
+The remote can immediately send an Offer using that derived binding while
+the responder has not committed its inbound binding yet.
+
+The receiver now waits only for the matching pending, cryptographically
+derived inbound binding to finish its native write, then revalidates the
+same active proven session and exact binding. Reset/disconnect releases
+waiters without authorizing retired sessions. Wrong bindings remain rejected.
+Outbound proof readiness is committed only after binding derivation finishes;
+duplicate capabilities no longer reset a proof response being written.
+No protocol/schema/signing/consent changes were made.
+
+Regression: removing the completion wait reproduces the exact binding error;
+restoring it persists a verified Offer without errors. A tampered binding is
+still rejected with the verified inbox remaining idempotent. Focused tests:
+79 passed, exit 0. Analyze/diff check exit 0. Full suite: 468 passed / 7 failed
+(the same two Chat fixture expiry errors and five BLE Test label expectations
+listed above), exit 1. Logs: `/tmp/offer_binding_focused2.log`,
+`/tmp/offer_binding_full_tests.log`, `/tmp/rescue_binding_race_before.log`.
+
+Android Debug and iOS Profile builds with existing production configuration:
+exit 0. A53 update-in-place install/launch completed, installed APK SHA-256
+matches `764fb70d85ac7e2cac4594ec5db7a8e55984b8ad1fbd720dfab07a74c3088de9`.
+B/iPhone and C/V2050 installation of this new build and physical reverse
+Offer/Chat confirmation remain pending. Existing misaddressed signed Chat
+records are retained; they are not silently rewritten or called delivered.
