+### Victim reply queued — confirmed self-recipient defect
+
+Operator reports C-to-A Chat reception, but A's reply remains Queued. A53
+read-only SQLite evidence for the current incident (masked `8b5645bb`):
+three outgoing local Chat messages have sender key equal to recipient key,
+both equal to the SOS origin. Durable Chat relay rows are failed with
+`A chat message ID is already used for different content`. The latest
+message is persisted locally and has a signed outbox envelope; this failure
+occurs before forwarding to B, during attempted local receive of its own row.
+No verified rescue offer exists in A's inbox for this incident (three verified
+offers belong to other incidents under the same owner).
+
+Source: `resolveVerifiedChatParticipant` fell back from a missing responder
+binding to the signed origin key even on the victim itself. It now detects
+the local origin identity and stops pending verified responder binding; the
+send callback cannot silently fall back to Direct BLE in that case.
+`signAndEnqueueChatRelay` also rejects a local recipient before creating any
+signed outbox row. Existing signed records are preserved and not silently
+rewritten or claimed sent. Focused resolver/three-node-persistence/direct
+coordinator tests: 42 passed. Analyze and diff check: exit 0.
